== 1. the contract
   basis.py: def is_measurement(source: BasisSource) -> bool:
   basis.py:     """Whether a basis source is a deposition's reading a run set
   basis.py:     (`measurement_source`): a deposition naming one reading,
   basis.py:     `<deposition id>/<entry id>`, its note saying when the reading was
   basis.py:     taken. A deposition naming a whole series (the readings a kinetic fit is
   basis.py:     made on, fermos.py) is the bench's record the fit rests on."""
   basis.py:     return (source.kind == "deposition" and bool(READING_REF.fullmatch(source.id or ""))
   basis.py:             and bool(_MEASURED.match(source.note or "")))
   ADR-006: - A reading's basis source is a `deposition` naming it (`basis.measurement_source`): its id the
   ADR-006:   ref, its `by` the depositor and its note `measured on <at>` with any conversion.
   ADR-006:   `basis.origin_of` reads it back as a `measurement`. A deposition source naming a whole series
   ADR-006:   (the readings a kinetic fit is made on) reads back as the bench's record, as it did, and the
   ADR-006:   fit's provenance stays what it was.
